{"OAuthLoginView uses pipeline.signature as the OAuth state value which is deterministic (md5 of pipeline view FQNs) rather than a per-session random nonce, weakening CSRF protection and allowing state replay across sessions": 0.8255146145820618, "GitHubInstallation assumes integration.metadata['sender']['login'] exists; if metadata.sender is missing or malformed (legacy data, partial state, or manual DB changes), this will raise KeyError/TypeError and 500 the flow instead of showing the failure dialog": 0.9475104212760925, "OAuthLoginView does not reliably handle exceptions from the GitHub /user call (which raises on non-2xx) and does not catch failures around the token exchange request, leading to 500s instead of the intended failure UI": 0.9297306537628174, "The OAuth authorize redirect URL is built via string interpolation rather than urlencode, which can create invalid URLs if values contain reserved characters and omits standard OAuth params like response_type=code": 0.6854695677757263, "GitHubInstallation queries Integration.objects.get(external_id=...) without filtering by provider, but Integrations are only unique on (provider, external_id), which can raise MultipleObjectsReturned or pick the wrong integration if IDs collide across providers": 0.6053735613822937}